  "avx512": "AVX-512 VNNI kernels are opt-in (--isa avx512vnni in ultra-engine-eval); evidence covers the live stream. Every release x86 binary (ultra-cold-wav, ultra, ultra-engine-commit) calls Isa::detect(), which picks AVX2/FMA on any x86 incl. AVX-512 hosts.",
  "batch": "live stream only (ultra-engine-eval --streams N decodes the N streams together each round); the commit pass decodes one segment at a time.",
  "final": "x86 (release ultra-engine-commit 9a142e8e, AVX2/FMA, on Zen 2 and on Xeon 8358) vs ARM (the same commit bb1071a built on Apple M3, NEON).",
  "neon_builds": "M3 binaries are built with --no-default-features (the wer scoring feature is Linux-only); ultra-cold-wav does not build on macOS."
